1
00:00:00,141 --> 00:00:02,672
I am Aaron, the first high priest of Israel.

2
00:00:03,918 --> 00:00:07,255
Once a year only once I went where no other

3
00:00:07,303 --> 00:00:08,876
man on earth was permitted to go.

4
00:00:10,343 --> 00:00:13,099
On that one morning I laid aside my garments

5
00:00:13,140 --> 00:00:13,440
of gold and glory.

6
00:00:15,249 --> 00:00:18,192
I washed my body with water, and I put on plain

7
00:00:18,312 --> 00:00:21,488
white linen, like a servant, like a man with

8
00:00:21,576 --> 00:00:22,546
nothing to boast of.

9
00:00:23,777 --> 00:00:25,971
And then I walked toward the veil with my heart

10
00:00:25,971 --> 00:00:26,271
in my throat.

11
00:00:27,864 --> 00:00:30,076
Behind that heavy curtain was the mercy seat,

12
00:00:30,498 --> 00:00:33,298
and above it, in the cloud, the presence of

13
00:00:33,339 --> 00:00:34,103
the living God.

14
00:00:35,652 --> 00:00:36,542
I went in alone.

15
00:00:37,689 --> 00:00:40,159
The whole nation stood outside, holding its

16
00:00:40,199 --> 00:00:43,319
breath and every year, as the curtain fell

17
00:00:43,399 --> 00:00:46,184
shut behind me, I was not certain I would come

18
00:00:46,244 --> 00:00:46,849
out alive.

19
00:00:48,495 --> 00:00:51,460
You who hear me I lost two of my own sons.

20
00:00:52,917 --> 00:00:55,791
Nadab and Abihu, my boys, were struck down

21
00:00:55,851 --> 00:00:58,641
before the LORD, for they offered strange fire

22
00:00:58,681 --> 00:01:00,743
before Him that He had not commanded.

23
00:01:01,989 --> 00:01:04,691
And I was not even allowed to mourn them: my

24
00:01:04,751 --> 00:01:06,843
cousins carried their bodies out of the camp,

25
00:01:07,145 --> 00:01:09,201
while I stood at the door of the tabernacle,

26
00:01:09,764 --> 00:01:12,450
forbidden to rend my clothes or leave my place.

27
00:01:13,916 --> 00:01:16,047
So when the LORD gave His warning concerning

28
00:01:16,107 --> 00:01:19,783
me, I did not take it lightly; I heard it in

29
00:01:19,844 --> 00:01:21,805
my bones every time I reached for the veil.

30
00:01:23,873 --> 00:01:26,387
The LORD spoke it to my brother Moses, and

31
00:01:26,448 --> 00:01:29,541
Moses brought me the word: Speak unto Aaron

32
00:01:29,682 --> 00:01:33,442
thy brother, that he come not at all times

33
00:01:33,623 --> 00:01:36,917
into the holy place within the vail before

34
00:01:37,002 --> 00:01:40,468
the mercy seat, which is upon the ark; that

35
00:01:40,488 --> 00:01:44,557
he die not: for I will appear in the cloud

36
00:01:44,838 --> 00:01:45,773
upon the mercy seat.

37
00:01:46,308 --> 00:01:49,024
That was my charge to stand at the veil for

38
00:01:49,052 --> 00:01:51,027
the people and not be consumed.

39
00:01:52,637 --> 00:01:55,586
Understand me: I did not bear their guilt.

40
00:01:56,517 --> 00:01:59,563
I could not; I had to bring blood for my own

41
00:01:59,684 --> 00:02:01,769
sin before ever I brought it for theirs.

42
00:02:02,934 --> 00:02:06,231
I only carried the blood in, and came out alive.

43
00:02:07,757 --> 00:02:09,850
For the law the LORD gave through Moses was

44
00:02:09,910 --> 00:02:12,931
plain, and it ran red through everything I

45
00:02:12,991 --> 00:02:16,252
did: for it is the blood that maketh an atonement

46
00:02:16,513 --> 00:02:17,112
for the soul.

47
00:02:17,112 --> 00:02:19,794
Something innocent had to die, or none of us

48
00:02:19,835 --> 00:02:20,135
could draw near.

49
00:02:22,045 --> 00:02:24,206
Let me tell you what I did with my own hands,

50
00:02:24,728 --> 00:02:27,170
for I did it year after year and could have

51
00:02:27,210 --> 00:02:28,141
done it in the dark.

52
00:02:29,348 --> 00:02:31,380
They brought me two goats for the people's

53
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:34,297
sin offering, and as the law of Moses commanded

54
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:37,417
I cast lots over them: And Aaron shall cast

55
00:02:37,598 --> 00:02:40,818
lots upon the two goats; one lot for the LORD,

56
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:43,350
and the other lot for the scapegoat.

57
00:02:43,435 --> 00:02:44,888
The first goat I killed.

58
00:02:45,675 --> 00:02:47,878
I took its blood in a basin and carried it

59
00:02:47,915 --> 00:02:50,688
where no ordinary man could follow through

60
00:02:50,728 --> 00:02:54,192
the veil, into the thick dark, and I sprinkled

61
00:02:54,212 --> 00:02:56,529
it before the mercy seat: Then shall he kill

62
00:02:56,589 --> 00:02:59,148
the goat of the sin offering, that is for the

63
00:02:59,188 --> 00:03:02,058
people, and bring his blood within the vail.

64
00:03:02,208 --> 00:03:03,981
But the second goat I did not kill.

65
00:03:04,909 --> 00:03:06,981
I laid both my hands upon its living head,

66
00:03:07,464 --> 00:03:10,134
and I confessed over it out of my own mouth

67
00:03:10,675 --> 00:03:13,114
all the wrong of all the people, and laid it

68
00:03:13,194 --> 00:03:15,531
upon the creature: And Aaron shall lay both

69
00:03:15,591 --> 00:03:18,591
his hands upon the head of the live goat, and

70
00:03:18,671 --> 00:03:21,912
confess over him all the iniquities of the

71
00:03:21,972 --> 00:03:25,026
children of Israel, and all their transgressions

72
00:03:25,690 --> 00:03:28,926
in all their sins, putting them upon the head

73
00:03:29,047 --> 00:03:32,329
of the goat, and shall send him away by the

74
00:03:32,389 --> 00:03:35,333
hand of a fit man into the wilderness.

75
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:37,399
And then I stood at the edge of the camp and

76
00:03:37,439 --> 00:03:40,774
watched it go, smaller and smaller, carrying

77
00:03:40,814 --> 00:03:42,873
it all away into a land where no one would

78
00:03:43,014 --> 00:03:45,390
ever find it: And the goat shall bear upon

79
00:03:45,451 --> 00:03:49,941
him all their iniquities unto a land not inhabited.

80
00:03:49,941 --> 00:03:52,120
Here is the thing that never let me rest.

81
00:03:53,065 --> 00:03:56,382
It was one sin offering yet it took two goats.

82
00:03:57,468 --> 00:03:59,971
The law of Moses said it plainly: And he shall

83
00:04:00,051 --> 00:04:02,428
take of the congregation of the children of

84
00:04:02,549 --> 00:04:05,614
Israel two kids of the goats for a sin offering.

85
00:04:06,354 --> 00:04:08,925
One I killed; the other I sent away alive.

86
00:04:09,926 --> 00:04:13,338
And I asked myself, year upon year: why two?

87
00:04:14,189 --> 00:04:15,601
Why not put both to death?

88
00:04:16,791 --> 00:04:19,615
One died to pay; the other lived to carry it

89
00:04:19,716 --> 00:04:22,236
off as though God meant to show two things

90
00:04:22,296 --> 00:04:24,883
at once that no single creature could hold.

91
00:04:26,351 --> 00:04:28,644
I performed it faithfully, and the riddle of

92
00:04:28,725 --> 00:04:29,307
it followed me home.

93
00:04:30,974 --> 00:04:32,928
And I will be honest with you, for an honest

94
00:04:32,995 --> 00:04:34,649
man must be honest before God.

95
00:04:35,856 --> 00:04:37,951
I obeyed, and I believed.

96
00:04:39,065 --> 00:04:41,980
The people went home clean for the LORD Himself

97
00:04:42,020 --> 00:04:44,420
had said that on that day they would be clean

98
00:04:44,481 --> 00:04:46,021
from all their sins before Him.

99
00:04:47,472 --> 00:04:48,643
That cleansing was real.

100
00:04:49,912 --> 00:04:51,304
And yet it was never the end.

101
00:04:52,391 --> 00:04:55,144
Every year the people sinned afresh, and every

102
00:04:55,184 --> 00:04:57,728
year I came back and did the whole thing again.

103
00:04:57,733 --> 00:05:01,248
A cleansing you must make again every year

104
00:05:01,409 --> 00:05:05,481
is true, but it is not finished; the need returned

105
00:05:05,541 --> 00:05:07,982
with each new year, as faithful as the feast.

106
00:05:09,676 --> 00:05:12,660
And in my old age a quiet fear pressed on me,

107
00:05:13,304 --> 00:05:16,483
one I dared not speak aloud at the altar: that

108
00:05:16,523 --> 00:05:19,385
for all the blood I poured out, I was only

109
00:05:19,545 --> 00:05:22,820
ever pointing pointing at some greater atonement

110
00:05:23,081 --> 00:05:24,903
that my own hands could never reach.

111
00:05:26,415 --> 00:05:27,084
I was a sign.

112
00:05:28,354 --> 00:05:29,807
I did not yet know of what.

113
00:05:30,555 --> 00:05:32,590
I did not see the answer in my own day.

114
00:05:33,678 --> 00:05:35,772
I tell you now looking back from the far side

115
00:05:35,819 --> 00:05:38,432
of my life by the light that came long after

116
00:05:38,538 --> 00:05:41,776
I laid down my office what every Day of Atonement

117
00:05:41,883 --> 00:05:43,598
was always reaching toward.

118
00:05:44,924 --> 00:05:47,879
That later word the letter to the Hebrews says

119
00:05:47,980 --> 00:05:50,987
plainly what I had only feared: that the blood

120
00:05:51,047 --> 00:05:52,878
I carried could never finish it.

121
00:05:52,984 --> 00:05:56,501
there is a remembrance again made of sins every

122
00:05:56,561 --> 00:05:56,861
year.

123
00:05:57,368 --> 00:06:00,104
For it is not possible that the blood of bulls

124
00:06:00,570 --> 00:06:03,126
and of goats should take away sins.

125
00:06:03,511 --> 00:06:06,386
It was a shadow and a shadow waits for the

126
00:06:06,435 --> 00:06:07,525
body that casts it.

127
00:06:08,858 --> 00:06:09,708
The body came.

128
00:06:10,715 --> 00:06:13,571
There came a Man, Jesus, and with His own blood

129
00:06:13,918 --> 00:06:16,274
He did what my basin of blood only pictured:

130
00:06:17,220 --> 00:06:19,556
He entered once, and it was finished.

131
00:06:20,705 --> 00:06:22,826
That same letter says of Him: Neither by the

132
00:06:22,846 --> 00:06:26,007
blood of goats and calves, but by his own blood

133
00:06:26,429 --> 00:06:29,910
he entered in once into the holy place, having

134
00:06:30,070 --> 00:06:32,341
obtained eternal redemption for us.

135
00:06:32,566 --> 00:06:35,321
By His own blood He paid the price bearing

136
00:06:35,361 --> 00:06:38,219
in His own death the judgment our sin had earned

137
00:06:39,122 --> 00:06:41,121
and He was the One upon whom the guilt was

138
00:06:41,181 --> 00:06:44,542
laid and carried clean away, as I had laid

139
00:06:44,562 --> 00:06:46,862
the people's sin on the goat I sent into the

140
00:06:46,923 --> 00:06:47,305
wild.

141
00:06:48,985 --> 00:06:51,560
Isaiah, the prophet who came after me, wrote

142
00:06:51,580 --> 00:06:54,600
it: and the LORD hath laid on him the iniquity

143
00:06:54,922 --> 00:06:55,222
of us all.

144
00:06:55,691 --> 00:06:56,722
That is why there were two.

145
00:06:57,469 --> 00:06:59,660
No single creature could show both halves at

146
00:06:59,781 --> 00:07:02,901
once the price paid and the guilt carried off

147
00:07:03,644 --> 00:07:05,808
and both were finished in one Priest.

148
00:07:07,234 --> 00:07:10,170
They led Him outside the city to die His body

149
00:07:10,256 --> 00:07:12,509
taken without the gate, as the sin offering's

150
00:07:12,569 --> 00:07:14,934
body was carried outside the camp and burned.

151
00:07:15,994 --> 00:07:19,112
The letter says: Wherefore Jesus also, that

152
00:07:19,192 --> 00:07:22,399
he might sanctify the people with his own blood,

153
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:24,462
suffered without the gate.

154
00:07:24,462 --> 00:07:26,523
And He did the one thing I never could.

155
00:07:27,472 --> 00:07:30,319
I always stood at my work; there was no chair

156
00:07:30,380 --> 00:07:31,145
behind that veil.

157
00:07:31,633 --> 00:07:33,927
But this Priest finished it, and sat down:

158
00:07:34,033 --> 00:07:37,608
But this man, after he had offered one sacrifice

159
00:07:37,628 --> 00:07:40,729
for sins for ever, sat down on the right hand

160
00:07:40,789 --> 00:07:41,089
of God.

161
00:07:40,889 --> 00:07:44,110
And the veil I trembled before the curtain

162
00:07:44,150 --> 00:07:47,177
that shut every man but one out, one day a

163
00:07:47,228 --> 00:07:51,572
year was torn the very hour He died, by no

164
00:07:51,752 --> 00:07:52,435
human hand.

165
00:07:54,097 --> 00:07:56,600
Matthew, in his gospel, records it: And, behold,

166
00:07:57,083 --> 00:08:00,668
the veil of the temple was rent in twain from

167
00:08:00,708 --> 00:08:02,058
the top to the bottom.

168
00:08:02,162 --> 00:08:05,480
So hear me and be still a moment, for this

169
00:08:05,480 --> 00:08:08,063
is the thing I waited my whole life to understand.

170
00:08:09,490 --> 00:08:10,701
Do not come to me.

171
00:08:11,991 --> 00:08:14,753
Do not come to a goat, or a yearly altar, or

172
00:08:14,794 --> 00:08:17,436
a priest in linen who is himself a dying man

173
00:08:17,778 --> 00:08:19,830
and must wash before he dares draw near.

174
00:08:21,139 --> 00:08:22,892
None of it ever stayed done.

175
00:08:24,376 --> 00:08:24,822
He can.

176
00:08:25,952 --> 00:08:28,688
Come to Jesus the High Priest who finished

177
00:08:28,729 --> 00:08:29,029
it.

178
00:08:29,977 --> 00:08:32,539
If you will come to Him, your sin is not held

179
00:08:32,599 --> 00:08:36,117
down for another year it is carried away, into

180
00:08:36,183 --> 00:08:39,250
a land not inhabited, as far as the east is

181
00:08:39,306 --> 00:08:41,841
from the west, never to be counted against

182
00:08:41,882 --> 00:08:42,284
you again.

183
00:08:43,645 --> 00:08:46,287
So David sang in his psalm, long before: As

184
00:08:46,387 --> 00:08:49,711
far as the east is from the west, so far hath

185
00:08:49,752 --> 00:08:52,084
he removed our transgressions from us.

186
00:08:52,410 --> 00:08:55,165
The veil I trembled before is torn, and no

187
00:08:55,226 --> 00:08:56,846
hand will ever sew it shut again.

188
00:08:56,846 --> 00:09:01,071
The way in is thrown wide open not for one

189
00:09:01,071 --> 00:09:02,404
man one day a year, but for you.

190
00:09:06,186 --> 00:09:08,628
That same letter says: Having therefore, brethren,

191
00:09:09,050 --> 00:09:12,354
boldness to enter into the holiest by the blood

192
00:09:12,576 --> 00:09:13,142
of Jesus.

193
00:09:13,268 --> 00:09:15,261
You do not need a priest like me to go in for

194
00:09:15,261 --> 00:09:15,594
you any longer.

195
00:09:17,571 --> 00:09:20,106
So I ask you the question I asked myself behind

196
00:09:20,171 --> 00:09:22,846
that veil, every year, with my heart in my

197
00:09:22,927 --> 00:09:26,288
throat only now there is no fear left in it:

198
00:09:27,639 --> 00:09:28,387
will you come in?

199
00:09:29,757 --> 00:09:32,149
Not when you are clean enough, not next year,

200
00:09:32,612 --> 00:09:36,529
not by your own blood but now, on His.

201
00:09:37,744 --> 00:09:38,044
Come.

202
00:09:39,039 --> 00:09:41,344
Trust the One who finished what I only ever

203
00:09:41,424 --> 00:09:42,045
foreshadowed.

204
00:09:43,070 --> 00:09:47,961
Walk in the holiest is open, and Jesus is already

205
00:09:47,961 --> 00:09:48,261
inside.
